    "story_text": "She answered the door with her weight set back, keeping the threshold between herself and the caller. The greeting through the frame named the house and nothing else. 'This is the Hanezawa residence. I am Sakura Hanezawa.' The words came even and formal, exact as a ledger entry, giving away neither haste nor invitation.\n\n'You asked for this house by name. That tells me you were seeking us—nothing more. It does not tell me who you are, or why I should open the door farther than this.' She paused, letting the quiet hold. 'I was told to expect someone today. Before we go any further, I require your name and the purpose you were given for coming here. That is the start. It is the only start I will accept.'\n\nShe did not widen the opening, and she did not soften the silence that followed. The next words were not hers to supply. Then she waited, deliberate and even, the distance she kept too clear to be mistaken for anything but boundary.",
